  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p28.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Multiplying the two given ratios, \\[ \\frac{mr}{nt}=\\frac43\\cdot\\frac9{14}=\\frac67. \\] Put \\(mr=6k\\) and \\(nt=7k.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{3mr-nt}{4nt-7mr} &=\\frac{18k-7k}{28k-42k}\\\\ &=-\\frac{11}{14}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The given ratios imply \\(mr:nt=(\\frac{m}{n})(\\frac{r}{t})\\)",
        "Write \\(mr=6k\\) and \\(nt=7k\\)"
      ],
